<section class="ex-note" id="overview">
<h2>1. Overview &amp; Comparison（總論與三病比較）</h2>
<ul>
<li>Endemic treponematoses 是與梅毒病原 <em>Treponema pallidum</em> 親緣很近的微生物所致的感染：<strong>pinta</strong>（<em>Treponema carateum</em>）、<strong>yaws</strong>（<em>T. pallidum</em> ssp. <em>pertenue</em>）、<strong>bejel</strong>（<em>T. pallidum</em> ssp. <em>endemicum</em>）。<span class="ex-ref">p.3173</span></li>
<li>與梅毒的重要差異：nonvenereal 傳染、只在特定地區流行（endemic）、傾向侵犯兒童而非性活躍成人、congenital transmission 的風險較低。<span class="ex-ref">p.3173</span></li>
<li>與梅毒相同：都會經過 early stage（含 primary 與 secondary）、latency、late stage；病程進展的併發症主要侵犯 skin、bone、cartilage，造成毀容、疼痛、失能與社會孤立。<span class="ex-ref">p.3173</span></li>
<li>WHO 在 <strong class="ex-n">1952–1964</strong> 年的全球計畫治療超過 <strong class="ex-n">50 million</strong> 人（特別針對 yaws），發生數減少 <strong class="ex-n">95%</strong>（從 50 million 降到 2.5 million）；之後防治交給地方基層醫療，監測鬆懈導致 <strong>resurgence</strong>。<span class="ex-ref">p.3173</span></li>
<li>近期研究估計至少 <strong class="ex-n">89 million</strong> 人住在 yaws 流行區；WHO 現將所有 endemic treponematoses 列為 <strong>neglected tropical diseases</strong>，目前目標是在 <strong class="ex-n">2020</strong> 年前消除（eliminate）yaws。<span class="ex-ref">p.3173</span></li>
</ul>
<table class="ex-table">
<thead><tr><th scope="col">Feature</th><th scope="col">Pinta</th><th scope="col">Yaws</th><th scope="col">Bejel</th></tr></thead>
<tbody>
<tr><td>Etiology</td><td><em>Treponema carateum</em></td><td><em>Treponema pallidum</em> ssp. <em>pertenue</em></td><td><em>Treponema pallidum</em> ssp. <em>endemicum</em></td></tr>
<tr><td>World distribution, main areas</td><td>Probably present focally in Brazilian and Venezuelan green forest</td><td>Papua New Guinea, Solomon Islands, and Ghana</td><td>African Sahel and Saudi Arabia</td></tr>
<tr><td>Climate conditions</td><td>Tropical green forest</td><td>Tropical humid</td><td>Hot and dry climate</td></tr>
<tr><td>Population affected</td><td>Children and adults</td><td>Mostly children</td><td>Mostly children</td></tr>
<tr><td>Transmission</td><td>Close contact</td><td>Close contact</td><td>Close contact and fomites</td></tr>
<tr><td>Primary lesion</td><td>Evident, can be multiple, several locations</td><td>One to several, lower extremities</td><td>Rarely evident</td></tr>
<tr><td>Predominant lesion</td><td>Vitiligo-like and hyperchromic lesions</td><td>Exudative, papillomatous or papulosquamous lesions</td><td>Moist lesions near mucosal surface or intertriginous areas</td></tr>
<tr><td>Nonskin involvement</td><td>None</td><td>Periostitis, osteitis</td><td>Periostitis, osteitis</td></tr>
